# AI Healthcare Chatbot 🩺

A Streamlit-based general health Q&A assistant powered by [OpenRouter](https://openrouter.ai),
letting you swap between multiple LLMs (Llama, GPT-4o mini, Claude, Gemini, etc.) without
changing code.

## Features

- 💬 Conversational general health Q&A (not a diagnostic tool)
- 🔀 Switch between multiple models via OpenRouter from a dropdown
- 📚 Sidebar "Quick Topics" for one-click common questions
- 🚨 Built-in emergency-language detection that surfaces crisis/emergency resources
  instead of a normal chatbot reply
- 📄 Export the full conversation as a PDF transcript
- ⚠️ Persistent medical disclaimer throughout the UI

## Project Structure

```
ai-healthcare-chatbot/
├── app.py              # Streamlit entry point / UI
├── chatbot.py           # OpenRouter API calls, system prompt, emergency detection
├── disease_data.json    # Quick-topic prompts shown in the sidebar
├── pdf_generator.py     # Builds a PDF transcript of the chat
├── requirements.txt
├── .env                 # Your OpenRouter API key (not committed)
└── README.md
```

## Setup

1. **Clone / open the project folder** and create a virtual environment:
   ```bash
   python -m venv .venv
   source .venv/bin/activate   # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
   ```

2. **Install dependencies:**
   ```bash
   pip install -r requirements.txt
   ```

3. **Add your OpenRouter API key.** Get one at https://openrouter.ai/keys, then edit `.env`:
   ```
   OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
   OPENROUTER_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.1-8b-instruct:free
   ```

4. **Run the app:**
   ```bash
   streamlit run app.py
   ```

5. Open the URL Streamlit prints (usually `http://localhost:8501`).

## Changing the model

Pick a model from the sidebar dropdown, or change the default in `.env` /
`MODEL_OPTIONS` in `app.py`. Any model slug supported by OpenRouter can be used —
see the full list at https://openrouter.ai/models.

> **Using a `:free` model and getting a 404?** OpenRouter's free-tier models require
> you to opt in to their data policy first. Go to https://openrouter.ai/settings/privacy
> and enable "free model publication" (prompt logging/training). Paid models like
> `openai/gpt-4o-mini` don't need this.
>
> Model slugs also get deprecated/renamed over time — if a model stops working, check
> https://openrouter.ai/models for its current slug.

## Important Disclaimer

This chatbot provides **general health information only**. It does **not**:
- Diagnose medical conditions
- Prescribe medication or dosages
- Replace a consultation with a licensed healthcare provider

For urgent or emergency symptoms, contact your local emergency services immediately.
If the app detects language suggesting a possible emergency (e.g. chest pain, suicidal
thoughts), it will show emergency resources instead of a conversational answer.

## Possible Extensions

- Dockerize the app for easier deployment
- Add unit tests for `chatbot.py` and `pdf_generator.py`
- Add authentication / per-user chat history persistence
- Add a symptom-checker mode alongside the Q&A mode